# Rust
# No trailing slash: `/target/` matches only a DIRECTORY, so a target/ that
# has been symlinked onto another disk shows up as untracked and can be
# committed by `git add -A` — as an absolute path to somebody's mount point.
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Local env
.env
.env.*

# tools/quickstart.sh — a throwaway laptop cluster's state, logs and inventory
/.flint-quickstart/

# Private keys, all of them. minisign.pub is committed on purpose; its secret
# half never is, nor is any CA or leaf key a drill happens to mint in the tree.
# Belt and braces, so a keypair generated here by accident cannot be staged.
# See docs/release-signing.md.
*.key
